      "id": "bug-phase4g-004",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-16T00:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "DashClaw approval endpoint returning 500 UNDEFINED_VALUE on POST /api/approvals/{id}",
      "file": "apps/fbis-mcp-server/tools/risk.py",
      "root_cause": "Three separate issues: (1) GET /api/approvals/{id} returns 405 — correct method is POST. (2) Decision values must be 'allow'/'deny' not 'approved'/'rejected'. (3) 'reasoning' field must be a string (even empty) — if omitted, it becomes undefined in DB query, causing postgres UNDEFINED_VALUE error. (4) Endpoint requires x-org-role: admin and x-user-id headers for human operator simulation.",
      "fix": "Updated _claw_wait_for_approval() to poll GET /api/actions/{action_id} for status changes (pending_approval→running=approved, →failed=denied) rather than trying to GET /api/approvals/. Human operator approves via POST /api/approvals/{id} with {decision: 'allow', reasoning: ''} + x-org-role: admin header. Full E2E test: guard→require_approval, create action→pending_approval, programmatic approval→running, outcome update→completed. ALL 6 STEPS PASS.",
      "tags": [
        "dashclaw",
        "hitl",
        "approval",
        "phase4g",
        "py",
        "e2e-validated",
        "prod-validated"
      ],
